      "dom_id": "question-71586",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=(x+y+z)^{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ (x+y+z)^{2} & =c \\\\ x+y+z & =\\pm \\sqrt{c} \\\\ x+y+z\\pm \\sqrt{c} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y,z)$ can't be negative. Therefore, we get a family of planes:\n\n$$\nx+y+z\\pm \\sqrt{c}=0,\\,c\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$",
